  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state received $65.7M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 282 awards, with an average award size of $233K, and obligations fell 99.3% year over year. FY27 obligations are partial, fiscal year to date, and follow full-year totals of $11.9B in FY22, $12.5B in FY23, $12.3B in FY24, $10.4B in FY25, and $9.2B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date buying at $40M. The Department of the Treasury is the next largest buyer at $17.9M. Procurement in FY2027 to date is concentrated in a handful of vendors and industries, with the largest vendor and industry each at $17.9M. Readers should note that the current-year totals are partial and represent obligations recorded so far in FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in Kentucky in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $40M in obligations. The Department of the Treasury follows with $17.9M and the Department of Justice follows with $6.9M. WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC is the largest vendor with $17.9M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest industry with $17.9M. The top buyers and top vendors together represent a large share of the $65.7M total obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What do FY2027 to date vendor and industry leaders look like?",
        "body": "WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC leads vendors at $17.9M, followed by UNIVERSITY OF LOUISVILLE at $7.5M and VALOR HEALTHCARE INC at $4.8M. The leading industries are Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $17.9M and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools at $7.8M. Couriers and Express Delivery Services appear with $4.2M, and All Other Outpatient Care Centers appear with $4.8M, showing a mix of manufacturing, education, and health-related procurement."
      }
    ]
  },
